as wrong and is withdrawn.\n- **Recorded frames:** the fixture holds tracking frames only, no calibration frames.\n- **New tool:** `gscript.replace_object` (`GObject.Replace` 632A402) swaps which VI a subVI node calls. On a scratch copy of S1 it scored 21/0: all wires kept, ExecState 1, handle count flat over 20 swaps. The swapped node gets a new uid (6810 → 23006), so every before/after comparison must map it back first. This also answers ROT's open item O6.\n\n**Decided (in `docs/m8-real-run-plan.md`):**\n- **Pre-decided 13:** the test swaps whole subVI nodes, not wires. `#6810` and `#22692` are replaced by replay VIs in dated copies of S1 and S3. Both copies run, and their X/Y/Z must match bit for bit, compared frame by frame.\n- **Pre-decided 14:** the prior-art review caught two errors in 13, both now fixed.\n  - I had named a `Buffer Number Out` terminal that `#6810` doesn't have.\n  - My predicted check could never fail, because `computation_diff` can't see which VI a node calls. It is replaced by three checks that can fail: wire diff empty, only the two swapped nodes changed, and ExecState 1.\n  - Each replay VI is a byte copy of the VI it replaces, edited inside, so its terminals match exactly.\n- **Pre-decided 15:** the swap tool is accepted, with the uid remap required before any comparison.\n\n**Next cycle's first act** (`tools/bench/next.json`, valid; STATUS NEXT rewritten): build `claudeDev\\replay\\replay_get_buff_image.vi` and `replay_get_image_cal.vi` through the staged pipeline. To pass, asking for frame 5 or frame 10049 must both return recorded frame 5.\n\n**Retrospectives:**\n- Cycle 74's retrospective had been left without a disposition; I wrote it first.\n- Cycle 75's retrospective ran to its END line (rc=0) and is dispositioned. It found one fault, `device-failed`, costing 0 min: `tools/logclass.py` counts a fact-review log as a build log. The repair is carried in STATUS.\n\n**Still owed next cycle:**\n- The fact review `archive/peer/2026-09-